-- title:
--   Injectivity and p-power cofinal image of ρ̄_* on Cartier modules
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and $\iota$ a ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}=W(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})$ to $W(k)$; write $j$ for the composite of $\iota$ with reduction modulo the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\Phi$ be a formal $O_D$-module over $W(k)/pW(k)$, i.e. a commutative two-variable formal group law with a $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$-action and an endomorphism $\varpi$ satisfying $\varpi\circ\varpi=[p]$ and $\varpi\circ a=\sigma(a)\circ\varpi$, subject to: $\Phi$ is special for $j$ (its Lie algebra is the internal direct sum of the $j$- and $j\circ\sigma$-eigenspaces, both invertible modules), $[p]=\Phi.\mathrm{act}(p)$ has kernel of degree $p^4$, the $j$-eigenspace of the Lie algebra lies in the kernel of the linear part of $\varpi$, and the degree $0$ and degree $1$ graded pieces of the Cartier module of $\Phi$ (the subgroups on which the Teichmüller action agrees with homothety by $j(\tau(c))^{p^n}$) are complementary, giving graded Cartier module data with attached $N$-module. Let $r_\Phi$ be an additive map from $\mathbb{Z}_p^{2}$ to that $N$-module which, for every canonical $L$-map $L$, maps the whole of $\mathbb{Z}_p^{2}$ bijectively onto the degree $0$ $\eta$-piece of $L$. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra in which $p$ is nilpotent, $\psi'\colon W(k)\to K$ a ring homomorphism, and $t'=(X,n,\rho)$ a rigidified object over $K$ which is admissible for $(\iota,\psi')$: $X$ is special for $\psi'\circ\iota$, $[p]$ on $X$ has kernel of degree $p^4$, and $\rho$ is an isogeny of height $4n$ from the base change of $\Phi$ along $\psi'$ to the reduction $\bar X$. Assume further that after base change along the localisation map $K\to K[1/1]$ the degree $0$ and degree $1$ graded pieces are complementary for $X$, for $\bar X$ and for $\bar\Phi$, and let $L'$ be a canonical $L$-map for the graded Cartier module data of $X$ over $K[1/1]$. Then the additive map $\bar\rho_*$ on Cartier modules induced by the base-changed reduction of $\rho$, from that of $\bar\Phi$ to that of $\bar X$, satisfies: there is $h\in\mathbb{N}$ such that $p^h\cdot m$ lies in the image of $\bar\rho_*$ for every $m$ in the Cartier module of $\bar X$, and $\bar\rho_*$ is injective.
--
--   This is the Cartier-module form of the statement that an isogeny of special formal modules over an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ becomes, after applying the Cartier functor, an injection with image containing $p^h$ times everything; the cokernel bound is the Manin-type degree formula for the length of the quotient by the image. It feeds the comparison of $\eta$-pieces under $\bar\rho_*$ used in the rigidification step of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.exists_nsmul_etaRed_nVarpi_eq_nMap_rhoC_of_mem_etaPiece_of_isAlgClosed_uniform`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.SpecialFormal.Rigidified.exists_nsmul_etaRed_nVarpi_eq_nMap_rhoC_of_mem_etaPiece_of_isAlgClosed_uniform).
